WEBVTT

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:14.780
Thirty million!

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.280
Richard...

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.010
<u>Episode 7</u>
<b>The Jade of Succession</b>

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.300
<b>One Week Earlier</b>

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.300
I'll be counting on you.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:06.060
Certainly.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.060
Seigi, this is Ito-sama of 
the Ito Shobin Company.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.570
Hello. It's nice to meet you.

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:14.530
Likewise.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:15.560
Well, then...

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.550
The Ito Shobin Company?

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:27.210
Seigi, are you free next Friday?

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:29.770
I'd like you to accompany me to an auction.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:30.830
An auction?

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:38.420
You mean an auction like you see
 on TV and in the movies?

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.270
Is something incredible going up for sale?

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:46.580
Yes. The collection of Azuma Soichi, 
who passed away last month.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.730
Also known as the Azuma Collection.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:57.270
Azuma was a managing director 
with profound cultural knowledge.

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.210
His massive collection made him

00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:02.920
one of Japan's most prominent 
collectors of gemstones and antiques.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.920
But since his passing, there's been a bit

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.690
of commotion surrounding
 the inheritance of his fortune.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.050
I can imagine.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.020
His eldest daughter, the new 
director of the Azuma family,

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:17.620
came up with a clever solution:

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:22.970
entrust her father's collection 
to an auction company

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.470
and liquidate all of it.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.960
That's rather drastic.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.490
I believe it's wiser than causing
 unnecessary discord within the family.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.230
Yeah, I guess so.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.790
Oh, right! Tea?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.410
This is the collection that's to be auctioned.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.140
This is all the Azuma Collection?

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:52.000
Yes.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.420
The most eye-catching piece 
is the Buddha's hand citron.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.630
Buddha's hand...?

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:59.030
Take a look at lot number 865.

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.590
So this is read "Buddha's hand citron"?

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.160
It's a 200-year-old jade piece

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:11.020
from the reign of the
 Qing Dynasty's Qianlong Emperor.

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:12.730
It's 200 years old?

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.660
I was asked to win this piece at the auction.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.910
You mean by that guy just now?

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:19.730
Yes.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:24.530
The Ito Shobin Company is a 
well-established antique shop in Ginza.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.210
The Japanese word for jade 
comes from the kingfisher.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.870
Because kingfishers are 
sometimes called "shobin,"

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:32.370
the characters for jade can 
also be read as "shobin."

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.120
The founder of the Shobin Company 
was so enamored by jade

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:39.800
that he named his store after it.

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:42.980
And this piece ended up 
in Azuma-san's possession.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.890
Upon Azuma's passing, he was intent 
on buying it back if at all possible.

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:54.140
Then why not buy it himself?
Why is he hiring you?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:59.240
The Shobin Company has been 
banned from the auction hall.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.530
Banned? Why?

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:05.050
Even after the collection was entrusted 
to the auction company,

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:08.970
Ito repeatedly offered to buy the 
Buddha's hand citron for a high price,

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:11.250
which compromised his reputation.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.350
So he then turned to an 
acquaintance of his, my mentor,

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:18.540
who passed the request along to me.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.010
A mentor? Richard, you have a mentor?

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.970
Is it that strange?

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.050
Er, well, no.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:29.460
Seigi, if you're available, will you 
accompany me to the preview, as well?

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.760
The preview?

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:35.820
It's an opportunity to see the 
objects for auction in person.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.480
Even the Buddha's hand citron?

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.810
Of course.

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:52.300
The Buddha's hand citron is a fruit
thought to bring good luck in China.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.570
Its shape resembles the Buddha's hand.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:57.960
It really does. 
You said it's 200 years old, right?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:03.960
It's been handled with care by so many 
different people since long before I was born...

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:08.050
But it looks more like an emerald than jade.

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:10.770
Jade isn't normally this translucent, right?

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.290
Good for you.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.470
You're developing an eye for gemstones.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:19.860
Highly translucent, blue-green 
jade is called jadeite.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:21.360
It's highly valued.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:24.330
So this one's top class.

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.160
Th-Thirty million?!

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.320
Quiet.

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.670
Er, sorry.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:32.130
This is the estimated sale price.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.710
The starting price should be much lower.

00:06:34.710 --> 00:06:36.160
Wow...

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.360
Richard...

00:06:48.850 --> 00:06:50.140
Huh?

00:06:50.140 --> 00:06:51.220
Richard?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.020
What a coincidence.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:58.230
I didn't expect to see you here,
 Lord Claremont.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.730
You have the wrong man.

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:07.300
Ah, come to think of it, I heard you go by 
Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian now.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.970
Are you looking to buy the jade hand, too?

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:14.450
Were you hired by a Frenchman? 
Or perhaps an Englishman?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:20.460
If you have business with the owner,
 I'll hear what you have to say.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:24.460
"The owner"? You work for him?

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.210
That's right.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.200
I forgot to introduce myself.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.600
My name is Shin Ganapati Bertuccio.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.480
I'm Nakata—

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.310
You needn't give him your name.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:50.200
Obstruction of business is 
your specialty, Lord Claremont.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:52.630
How truly amusing.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.580
Did you give up on finding happiness 
with your fellow countryman

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:58.340
and choose a foreigner instead?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:01.410
You don't know me.

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:06.960
You there... Stay with him too long,
and you'll be met with disaster.

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.890
Be careful.

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:13.010
Well, Lord Claremont, 
give my regards to Ranashinha.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.130
Ranashinha?

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.490
You're... not okay, are you?

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:26.970
I regret that you had to see that.

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:28.520
I apologize.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:32.660
He was a former competitor of mine.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:36.990
He would frequently claim 
that I stole his customers.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:42.530
<i>As long as you're selling it, 
your customers would buy plain stone.</i>

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:45.680
<i>They're too enchanted by your face 
to look at what's in their hands.</i>

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.070
It was a troublesome time.

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:52.080
Where you used to work before...
Was it your mentor's store?

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:53.000
Yes.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.210
My mentor operates the 
main store in Sri Lanka.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.980
There's a second store in Hong Kong,

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:01.350
and the third is Étranger here in Tokyo.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:05.600
So who's this "Ranashinha" he just mentioned?

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:09.780
Saul Ranashinha, my mentor.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:13.320
Is he a relative or something?

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:17.860
No. Due to certain circumstances, 
I'm borrowing his name.

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:19.630
We have no blood relation.

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.230
Any other questions?

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.870
No, it's fine. You've already told me plenty.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.250
Thank you.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.590
I appreciate your consideration.

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.510
You're a very kind person.

00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:42.580
You're like a man drawing 
his face in just before a kiss.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:44.140
What? A kiss?

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:52.150
I just meant that it's fine if there are 
things you don't want to tell me.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:55.400
Are you a philanthropist or a coward?

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:58.900
It's difficult to decipher.

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.200
It doesn't matter either way!

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:04.430
I just hate guys who try to force themselves

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:08.420
on people who don't want to be kissed!

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:14.050
Oh, uh...

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:20.470
In other words, I don't want to 
force you to do anything.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:25.470
I like you, and I owe you.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.490
What? Don't look at me like that.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:35.610
Sorry... I just realized 
how you really feel about me.

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:39.950
Did I really have to say it
 out loud for you to get it?

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.830
I'm grateful.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:46.500
You're right. I should tell you myself.

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:50.110
Richard...

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:55.750
Don't get the wrong idea. I'm not desperate.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:59.130
It just feels like it's the right time.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:02.760
But can it wait until after the auction?

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:05.370
Of course.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.850
If that man is here,

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:14.170
then there must be a buyer 
in Europe who wants this jade.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.240
Thirty million...

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:18.500
I'm not sure that will be enough.

00:11:18.500 --> 00:11:19.320
What?

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:22.780
It will be a fierce battle.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:42.010
I'm so sorry for asking you to do this.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:46.010
Will 30 million be enough?

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:47.720
I'm not sure.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.110
After hearing from Richard, 
we discussed the matter

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:52.800
and raised the upper limit, but...

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:03.280
What is it?

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:08.900
It's true that seeing something 
so beautiful can strike you dumb...

00:12:08.900 --> 00:12:12.050
You've become quite the smooth talker.

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:14.960
Richard, should I really be dressed like this?

00:12:15.390 --> 00:12:18.060
You're my bag boy, aren't you?

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:19.390
It's fine.

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:22.910
Will <i>that</i> be all right?

00:12:22.910 --> 00:12:25.550
Don't worry. Let's go.

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.960
"That"?

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:37.110
There's a ton of people.

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:40.700
The biggest draw is about to go up.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:44.780
You're dressed fabulously, Lord Claremont.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.670
That face...

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:48.880
No matter where you go,

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:52.120
no one who's ever associated 
with you could forget it.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:57.100
Your face is your business card.

00:12:57.100 --> 00:12:58.690
Poor you.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:00.650
I'm thanking the heavens.

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:07.300
Even someone like you who's so bad
 with names still remembers my face.

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:12.640
I am Richard Ranashinha de Vulpian.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:18.940
By the way, who is your client? 
What's your budget?

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:22.730
I haven't fallen so low 
as to discuss that with you.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:26.950
No matter who my client is, 
you don't stand a chance.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:32.200
Valuable objects end up in worthy hands.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:36.790
I will get what my client wants.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.420
It's royal milk tea flavored.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.980
For a chance of pace.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.050
Thank you.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.480
The afternoon auction will now resume.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.980
Lot number 800.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:06.490
Bidding for this ruby necklace 
will begin at three million.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:12.870
I have 3.1 million, 3.2 million, 3.3 million.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.770
Four million, 4.1 million.

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:17.580
Raising the paddle with your 
number on it constitutes a bid.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.110
Five million.

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:20.630
And when there's only one bidder left...

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:23.410
Sold for five million.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:26.030
I see.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:30.300
What? You want me to bid?

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:33.240
Aren't you my bag boy?

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:37.430
Yeah...

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.650
Lot number 865.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:43.610
The Buddha's hand citron.

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:51.240
A jade piece from the reign of the 
Qing Dynasty's Qianlong Emperor.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.790
Bidding will start at ten million.

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:00.080
Eleven million.

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:02.190
Twelve million.

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.090
Thirteen million.

00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:05.750
Twenty million!

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:09.760
Twenty-one million. Twenty-two million.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:11.260
Thirty million!

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:12.760
Thirty million...

00:15:13.190 --> 00:15:16.390
Thirty-one million. Thirty-two million.

00:15:16.760 --> 00:15:19.260
Is it okay to keep ours up?

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.220
Thirty-three million. Thirty-four million.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:20.140
Of course.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:29.250
Thirty-five million. 
Thirty-six million. Thirty-seven million.

00:15:29.250 --> 00:15:31.860
This is all you can afford.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.100
Thirty-eight million.

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:41.210
Thirty-nine million. Forty million!

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:44.420
Forty-one million.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:47.460
How much more can you pay?

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.670
Forty-one and a half million.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:54.640
Forty-two million. Forty-two and a half.

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.650
Look sharp.

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:56.550
R-Right!

00:15:56.550 --> 00:16:01.060
Forty-three million. Forty-three and a half.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:08.350
Forty-four million. Forty-four and a half.
Forty-five million.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:15.600
Sold for 45 million.

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:19.320
You can put it down now.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:21.910
Huh? O-Oh...

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:24.960
Well done.

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:34.370
Your budget was supposed to 
be 30 million and change!

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:38.300
So you were spying to determine my budget.

00:16:39.810 --> 00:16:44.770
You're a cursed man! 
You'll bring misfortune again!

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.940
It's none of your concern 
whether he does or not!

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:51.360
Stop interfering with his business!

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:55.950
You're blinded by someone you don't 
even realize is poison, you fool!

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:06.110
Richard-san!

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:12.300
Ito-san, Richard-san! Thank you so much!

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.550
I'm Azuma Hidenori.

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:22.490
Azuma? You're a member of the Azuma family?

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:23.310
Wait!

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:26.030
You three know each other?!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:32.070
So Azuma-san was the other investor.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:36.800
Yes. Because Hidenori-san 
agreed to invest ten million,

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:39.780
we managed to scrape together 40 million.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.960
But the final price was 45 million, right?

00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:45.260
Who's covering the remaining five million?

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:48.220
Is it you, Richard?

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:51.040
I'm pleased that I was able to help.

00:17:51.040 --> 00:17:54.970
Help? Where are you going to get five million?

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:58.080
Thank you so much.

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:01.300
If it hadn't been for your 
investment, Richard-san,

00:18:01.650 --> 00:18:05.670
I would've cursed my aunt for putting 
the Buddha's hand citron up for auction.

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:08.310
Cursed her? You'd hate her that much?

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:09.710
Yes.

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:14.480
To me, the Buddha's hand citron is ripe 
with my memories of my grandfather.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.380
Ever since I was a child, 
I had trouble getting along

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:22.680
with the members of our main family.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:28.740
But my grandfather always let me 
handle that softly glowing jade.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:31.650
The Buddha's hand citron...

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:32.750
Yes.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:37.650
That's why I wanted to keep the 
Buddha's hand citron no matter what,

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.470
even if the rest of his fortune was lost.

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:45.720
If it made it overseas, it would have
 been difficult to track down again.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.510
Just like when the Qing Dynasty weakened,

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:51.180
other powerful nations purchased 
its jade at low prices,

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:53.480
scattering it around the world.

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:57.470
I wanted to avoid that.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:19:02.030
And if I may add, as someone
 who works in the world of gems,

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:06.870
I didn't want to doom that jade 
to wander any longer.

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:11.860
Our motives were different, 
but we had the same goal.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:19.970
This protrusion at the base represents a bat.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:24.970
Since ancient times, bats have been 
considered good luck in China.

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.420
A good luck charm...

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:31.810
A jade charm full of Azuma-san's 
memories of his grandfather...

00:19:32.930 --> 00:19:35.110
Oh, thank you.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:39.270
I bet Grandpa's smiling right now.

00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:42.450
He probably wasn't expecting his grandson 
to buy back one of his own possessions.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:59.510
Anyway, I'm surprised you had five million.

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:03.410
Naturally, I expect them to reimburse me.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:07.320
But if it means preserving the 
Azuma family, then it was a bargain.

00:20:07.320 --> 00:20:09.850
I-I don't think anyone would call that cheap.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.690
If money alone is enough to 
preserve it, then it is cheap.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:17.650
That means it can be destroyed
 over something so trivial.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.820
Let's continue our discussion 
from the other day.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:28.140
It's a boring story that takes place 
in the suburbs of London.

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:31.580
Your inheritance?

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:35.590
Yes. They're still arguing over 
the tremendous inheritance

00:20:35.590 --> 00:20:37.750
my grandfather left behind.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.390
The family had a falling-out.

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:43.340
People were betrayed by those 
they considered friends.

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:46.360
Romantic unions were broken up.

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:48.580
A lot happened.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:53.160
Should you be running 
a jewelry store in Japan?

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:55.930
What should I be doing instead?

00:20:56.640 --> 00:20:58.130
I see...

00:20:58.130 --> 00:21:01.150
In any case, thanks for telling me.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.030
You're welcome.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:07.160
This is probably the reason 
that man said what he did.

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:09.410
The reason?

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:14.850
Why he warned you that you'd 
be met with disaster if you

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:16.420
stayed with me too long.

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.520
That was a warning?

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:22.690
He was serious?
 That's just what happened to you.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:24.380
Give me a break.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:36.710
Well, I'm headed this way.
See you next week.

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:39.290
Yes, see you next week.

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:43.780
Seigi.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:47.050
Don't blame me if you regret it.

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:48.490
Regret what?

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:53.750
Saying that you like me.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:56.240
Farewell.
